<title>PERU: Peru's July cotton output falls 10.7 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru's July cotton output falls 10.7 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's July cotton production fell 10.7 percent to 25,083 tonnes, compared with the same month last year, the Agriculture Ministry said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Output in the first seven months rose 9.5 percent to 167,339 tonnes, compared with the same period in 1995, the ministry said.</p>
<p>Total 1995 production was 216,869 tonnes.</p>
<p>Imports of uncombed cotton in July fell 59.5 percent to 961 tonnes, worth $1.450 million, while imports in the first seven months dropped 43.9 percent to 6,366 tonnes, worth $10.659 million.</p>
<p>July cotton exports rose 71.1 percent to 1,020 tonnes, worth $2.387 million, while exports in the first seven months increased 180 percent to 5,867 tonnes, worth $16.950 million.</p>
<p>-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom 511 221-2134</p>
</text>
